      "key": "design_ontology",
      "label": "Accepted design Ontology"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "M(B), the complete material-relation set, comprises entities, identities, relationships, cardinalities, invariants, authorities, authority transitions, functions, higher-order composition laws, topology, lifecycle states/transitions, public contracts, externally observable Product meaning, declared domains/admission conditions, failure/refusal routes, effect/closure laws, projections, module mappings and material algorithmic obligations. U(B) = unresolved(M(B)). Decision completeness means U(B) is empty, M(B) is jointly satisfiable, and all networks it admits are semantically equivalent under governing Product, requirements and accepted design relations. co_evolution_admissible(B) iff decision_complete(B); design_gate(B) is the smallest causally closed affected set needed to establish it.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
