      "key": "calculus_position_boundaries",
      "statement": "Definitions do not depend on derivation-source layout, selected subject interpretation, carrier, provider, runtime or repository topology. Selected-cut F1–F6 and shared laws are operative premises; predecessor clauses are historical provenance. Signature, record kinds, closure operator and functor classification are this standard's additional owned choices, not uniquely derived from either source or finite capacity. Given explicit interpretation and typed subject, references must be resolved and compatible on one exact basis before consuming a model judgment. AC-007/014 consume the shared result algebra; AC-016 consumes conjunction for claims requiring several judgments. The transformation library supplies reusable responsibilities but neither replaces AC-013 nor establishes categorical functor laws. Universal applicability, completeness, consistency, decidability, soundness and categorical status are not asserted absent the stated proof exception.",
