      "key": "calculus_scope",
      "statement": "The calculus governs symbolic-model form: identities/types, exact relation endpoints, explicit constraints/latitude/residuals, traversal/judgment typing, closure/projection/overlay/transformation behavior, subject preservation, and separation of structural, semantic and authority claims. It does not choose vocabulary or material declarations, supply semantic acceptance, select a carrier, execute a model or prove unique interpretation.",
