      "conditions": [],
      "exceptions": ["An empty population is allowed only if the selected signature requires no member of its record kind."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 181,
          "quote": "Every `a_c` signature imports those identities unchanged. A model-family\nsignature specializes their fields, value domains, reference domains, and\nadmissible kinds; it does not remove, rename, shadow, or silently add a core\nrecord family. Another fundamental record family requires an explicit\ncompatible calculus extension rather than an extra subject sort.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#The%20STDO%20Axiomatic%20Calculus%20for%20Governed%20Symbolic%20Systems%2FCore%20Signature",
          "start_line": 177
        }
      ],
      "key": "signature_population_and_reference_contract",
      "statement": "Every signature imports all eight core identities unchanged; specialization closes fields/value domains, identity-reference domains/cardinalities, relation endpoint sorts, constraint subject/predicate domains, residual subject/uncertainty/consequence/re-entry domains, judgment input/output/evidence/stop contracts and permitted traversal kinds. Removing, renaming, shadowing or silently adding core families is prohibited; a new fundamental family requires explicit compatible calculus extension, not a subject sort. Unknown fields/kinds require a new signature or compatible extension relation. Population_M is total, finite and disjoint, with each fundamental record exactly once and globally unique identity. External_M identities require exactly one signature-declared external domain and exact resolution. Hidden records, unpopulated extra families, duplicated identities or identities lacking one lawful local/external resolution refuse the model. Every scalar/collection identity reference is checked by RefDomain_Sigma: exact target population, semantic sort when applicable, or exactly one external target kind/basis relation, never both local and external. Missing domains, wrong family/sort, ambiguity and dangling external identities refuse structural admission.",
