      "key": "proof_before_enforcement",
      "statement": "First parse/validate/construct; explicitly admit/narrow; then enforce proved shape. Relabeling open payloads, typed envelopes preserving loose authority, casts/unchecked assertions/dynamic mutation do not establish closure. The rule is language-neutral: strict typing, sealed ADT/parser or compiler sum type/decoder are examples of enforcement after proof.",
