          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4.%20Functional%20Bias%20Without%20Language%20Mandate",
          "start_line": 332
        }
      ],
      "key": "claimed_functional_boundary_duties",
      "statement": "Kernel is pure for identical admitted inputs. Time, randomness, UUID minting, environment/process/filesystem/network reads and registries belong to declared ingress/effect boundaries, with explicit identity-creation owner. Reject invalid/incomplete truth at ingress; local transforms use admitted carriers without reparsing/reloading locally assembled truth. Defaults are explicit, ratified and carrier-owned. Each function has one clear owner/responsibility; admission, semantics and effects cannot be mixed in convenience helpers. Algebra depends on carrier contracts, admission on validation, not runtime shells or orchestration; package/bootstrap/controller/adapter/runtime-shell layers stay below semantic center. Effect boundaries remain typed and preserve carrier truth.",
      "uncertainty": "The referenced justified-mutation cases are not supplied."
