    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["design_boundary"],
      "conditions": ["This method governs a Python boundary."],
      "exceptions": ["Narrow Any/cast/type-ignore uses are permitted only under all conditions in python_foreign_boundary_latitude."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 348,
          "quote": "When this method governs a Python boundary, repo-authored Python must be fully\ntyped.\n\nThat means:\n\n- every function, method, and callable surface has explicit parameter and return\n  annotations\n- semantic carriers are closed and typed\n- repo-authored tests, scripts, and support code are typed too; they do not get\n  a lower bar than production code",
