      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 592,
          "quote": "Evaluate preservation against every affected governing frame and update only\naffected subordinate projections. Changing an accepted governing relation\nrequires re-entry at that relation before acceptance. Open a subordinate frame\nonly for a material distinction unresolved at the governing altitude; neither\na closure algorithm nor recursive documentation of irrelevant descendants is\nrequired. A locally valid action that violates or silently reinterprets an\naffected governing invariant fails this obligation. Duplication follows\n[UP-018's action classification and explicit disposition](#invariant-reconstruction-sufficiency-stdo-up-018);\nan undisposed duplicate cannot establish preservation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FBounded%20Frame%20Conservation%20%28%60STDO-UP-017%60%29",
          "start_line": 584
        }
      ],
      "key": "bounded_frame_conservation",
      "statement": "Contract application/composition binding declares accepted governing frames, bounded affected relations, inherited invariants, crossing authority/composition seams and subordinate frames for unresolved material distinctions. Governance may be a network of lifecycle/consistency/admission/runtime/sibling consumers; seam closure needs causally relevant far-side relation or evidenced independence. Preserve every affected governing frame; update only affected subordinate projections; changing governing relation re-enters there before acceptance. Open subframes only for material unresolved distinctions; no mandated closure algorithm or irrelevant recursive documentation. Local validity cannot excuse violated/reinterpreted invariants; undisposed duplicates cannot establish preservation. Discovered verbs/screens/endpoints/commands/tickets/use cases are behavior evidence, not direct public-operation/carrier/module/function identities: derive through Ontology. Required order: constitutional functionality -> candidate Ontology -> logical completeness -> whole-family Prime contraction -> accepted Ontology -> IACS -> target design/domain-sequence-state views -> public contracts/adapters -> implementation/tests.",
      "uncertainty": "UP-018 action classes/disposition and shared support contract are not supplied in full."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["design_boundary"],
      "conditions": ["Design acceptance is claimed under native constructability."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 625,
          "quote": "A semantically coherent design is not acceptable when its selected substrate\ncannot natively construct the required identities, relationships, transitions,\nauthority boundaries, effects, lifecycle, composition, publication, and\nretirement behavior.\n\nA missing substrate capability remains an explicit design gap or triggers\nlawful re-entry. It must not be hidden behind a reference bridge, adapter,\nfilesystem runner, test double, or promised future feature. This is a\nconstructability obligation, not a prescribed implementation; the consumer\nchooses the substrate and evidence mechanism.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FNative%20Constructability%20Before%20Design%20Acceptance%20%28%60STDO-UP-002%60%29",
          "start_line": 616
        }
