    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["foundation_selection", "design_boundary"],
      "conditions": ["Before constructing a material algorithm/common mechanic/generic capability, selecting a material dependency, or retaining a newly exposed material generic subproblem."],
      "exceptions": ["No package survey/ledger is required for a trivial helper incapable of materially affecting authority, Product behavior, lifecycle cost or accepted design network."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 664,
          "quote": "Candidate discovery is bounded, reproducible, and explicitly non-exhaustive.\nFor every candidate category, the evidence record declares the sources or\ncollections searched, cutoff time and relevant version basis, applicability and\ninclusion criteria, material exclusions, predecessor or incumbent status,\ndiscovered candidates, and residual unknowns; a category not searched records\n`not_applicable` or a named gap with its reason. Discovery closes only for that\ndeclared basis and cutoff. A discovery gap that could materially alter the\nfrontier prevents selection; an immaterial residual records why it cannot change\nthe current decision. A later candidate that satisfies the applicability\ncriteria and could materially alter the lawful frontier invalidates the affected\nselection evidence and re-enters this relation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FCapability%20And%20Foundation%20Selection%20%28%60STDO-UP-023%60%29",
          "start_line": 654
        }
      ],
      "key": "foundation_discovery_scope",
      "statement": "Perform proportional selection first; describe capability without Product/domain/module/vendor/file/incumbent labels, separating irreducible semantic/authority roles with owner, kind, subject, scope, basis, lifecycle/refusal invariants from generic supporting mechanics. Factoring concerns roles, not authorship. For every candidate category record searched collections, cutoff/version basis, applicability/inclusion, exclusions, incumbent/predecessor status, candidates and residuals; unsearched category needs not_applicable or reasoned gap. Closure is only on that basis/cutoff. A potentially frontier-changing discovery gap prevents selection; immaterial residual explains why decision cannot change. Later applicable frontier-changing candidate invalidates affected evidence and re-enters. Stay inside Product and admitted migration strategy; do not choose bounded evolution versus fundamental readoption or override Spec presumption. Predecessor may constrain migration candidate set; discovery may start with incumbent but selection gives no source-order/familiarity/sunk-cost/local-code/dependency-count preference. Compare compositions, not just packages. Newly exposed material generic subproblems recursively re-enter before retained implementation; prior selection differs from later recurrence review.",
