          "quote": "- two materially non-equivalent admission relations remain reachable for the\n  same governed transition domain on the same entity identity, authority scope,\n  and predecessor basis — disjoint scopes or identities are not a\n  counterexample;\n- a materially equivalent competing implementation remains reachable without\n  being identified as a constituent, replica, replacement, or deliberately\n  independent realization; or\n- a projection-triggered reaction uses its own reconstructive state as\n  self-authenticating admission evidence.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FTransformation%20Admission%20Completeness%20%28%60STDO-UP-016%60%29",
          "start_line": 877
        }
      ],
      "key": "admission_singularity_and_projection_boundary",
      "statement": "Singularity attaches to complete decision relation, not one actor/callable/component; declared relations may require one actor, multiple signatures, quorum, human step-up, proxy delegation or jurisdictional partition. Competing-path disposition need not delete equivalent paths, but superseded responsibility retention requires distinct supported purpose under external Core Interface Migration Rule, not label/test alone. Projection can propose transformation but grants no admission authority; consequential result re-enters governing relation against explicit predecessor, never self-authenticating reconstructed state. Law is false when two materially nonequivalent paths remain reachable on same transition/entity/scope/predecessor, equivalent reachable implementations lack explicit relationship, or projector reactions self-authenticate. Stated exceptions retain lawful multiplicity.",
      "uncertainty": "Full external Core Interface Migration Rule is not supplied."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["design_admission_relation"],
      "conditions": ["Using the admission contract for a declared candidate and predecessor on a scoped entity."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 914,
          "quote": "A shape-correct projector candidate therefore requires authentic\ncurrent-predecessor support and the actual grant at this gate; those facts\nalone do not establish the remaining admission conditions. Unresolved seams\nuse UP-017's declared affected set under the shared support condition. Basis\nadvancement before semantic commit prevents the effect and requires UP-021\ncurrent-basis re-entry. This is the existing admission assessment, not an\nadditional validation pass.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FTransformation%20Admission%20Completeness%20%28%60STDO-UP-016%60%29%2FAdmission%20contract%20use",
          "start_line": 908
        }
      ],
      "key": "admission_contract_bindings",
      "statement": "Bind authoritative admission basis, complete relation/commit unit, required support, admitter grant and supported durable-result/other outcome under Contract application/admission specialization; these are semantic bindings, not new carrier. Method owns design completeness; UP-021 owns admission/standing tests, reason-sensitive mapping, missing/stale/incompatible/unusable basis, trust-boundary validation and separate assessment/authorized-decision/observed-commit predicates. Predecessor continuity/currentness/admitter authority are material joins. Preserve qualified outcome and performance/effects including nonperformance, partial publication and unknown effects. Candidate shape is different predicate. Shape-correct projector still needs authentic current-predecessor support and actual grant, insufficient alone for all admission conditions. Unresolved seams use UP-017 affected set. Basis advancement before semantic commit prevents effect and requires current-basis re-entry in existing assessment, not another validation pass.",
      "uncertainty": "UP-021's exact reason-sensitive map and standing tests cannot be reconstructed from the supplied references."
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["atomic_function_family", "design_ontology"],
      "conditions": ["The adopted boundary derives functions; higher-order requirements apply where such behavior exists."],
      "exceptions": ["Iterative discovery of composition/effects/implementation is allowed only when co_evolution_admissible(B); otherwise disposable spikes alone may supply preacceptance evidence across affected unresolved, contradictory or materially nonequivalent relations."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 935,
          "quote": "Every row must be one of:\n\n- derived through an admitted atomic function;\n- derived through a declared higher-order composition;\n- deferred with an owner and re-entry condition;\n- excluded by current product authority; or\n- unresolved as a named gap.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FAtomic%20Functions%20And%20Higher-Order%20Composition",
          "start_line": 929
        }
      ],
      "key": "function_derivation_and_composition",
      "statement": "Derive smallest lifecycle-complete parameterized families; differences only in entity/projection/transition kind, policy or subordinate payload should normally be typed parameters/closed variants rather than peers. Every minimum evidence row must be admitted-atomic-derived, declared-composition-derived, deferred with owner/re-entry, excluded by current Product authority, or named unresolved gap. Higher-order boundaries name composition/effect algebra and applicable identity, closure, associativity, cardinality, effect and authority-conservation laws explicitly. No mandatory monadic/category vocabulary; ODD may bind GTL/ABG, others explicit alternatives. Every retained result reconciles into accepted design before promotion/closure; no private helper, loop, adapter or endpoint becomes undeclared constructor.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["prime_semantic_atom"],
      "conditions": ["Prime acceptance/conformance is claimed under the adopted profile."],
      "exceptions": ["Out-of-domain cases may justify proposing a new candidate atom for design admission."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 980,
          "quote": "Every accepted Prime atom declares the admitted domain over which its law\nholds. Within that domain it governs every admitted instance. A later use case\ncomposes or parameterizes the atom; it does not fork, shadow, specialize, or\nreinterpret the atom locally. An out-of-domain case may justify proposing\nanother candidate atom for design admission. An in-domain counterexample\nfalsifies the shared atom and re-enters at that atom's design boundary rather\nthan authorizing a feature-local replacement.\n\nAn atom without a declared admitted domain remains a candidate atom. It cannot\nsupply Prime acceptance or Prime-conformance to a realization projection.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FPrime%20Semantic%20Atoms%20And%20Universal%20Domain",
          "start_line": 971
        }
      ],
      "key": "prime_domain_and_realization",
      "statement": "One atom may map to several units and one unit to several atoms with explicit mapping and no rival meaning/authority. Atomic functions are not proven Prime before whole-family contraction. Each accepted atom declares domain and governs every admitted instance therein; later use cases compose/parameterize, never locally fork/shadow/specialize/reinterpret. In-domain counterexample falsifies shared atom and re-enters its design boundary, not feature-local replacement. No declared domain means candidate only, incapable of granting Prime acceptance/conformance.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["prime_semantic_atom"],
      "conditions": ["Before promotion under whole-family Prime review."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 988,
          "quote": "Prime review evaluates the complete candidate semantic-atom family and every\nproposed realization projection, not only functions, carriers, or each atom in\nisolation. The family includes every proposed identity, authority transition,\nlifecycle relation, topology, function, composition law, effect, and closure\nlaw. A function-and-carrier-only pass does not establish whole-family Prime.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FWhole-Family%20Prime%20Contraction",
          "start_line": 984
        }
      ],
      "key": "whole_family_prime_review",
      "statement": "Review complete identity/authority-transition/lifecycle/topology/function/composition/effect/closure family and every realization projection, not isolated atoms or functions/carriers alone. Ask whether operations are parameters of one function, commands transitions of one entity, reads projections of one truth, implementations instances of higher-order function; whether independent identity/authority/effect/lifecycle/reuse/public-pattern-match semantics are introduced; whether every kind entered contraction; every unit maps to accepted atoms; and any projection duplicates/reinterprets/introduces meaning or authority. Plausible separate functions are not Prime if one parameterized template with closed variants preserves meaning/authority. Contract visible recurrence during design; postimplementation recurrence review is no substitute.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["prime_semantic_atom", "design_boundary"],
      "conditions": ["A material semantic boundary undergoes Prime contraction."],
      "exceptions": ["Work within accepted boundary cites existing Prime basis rather than recreating it."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1025,
          "quote": "Contraction must preserve root authority and every retained semantic relation.\nReducing files, functions, operations, or authoring surfaces cannot compensate\nfor introducing another authority source or truth path. Prime evidence states\nthe complete candidate semantic-atom family; each atom's stable identity,\nirreducible relation, admitted domain, and falsification condition; the\nwhole-family contraction relation; retained meaning and authority before and\nafter contraction; accepted loss; and the explicit total mapping from every\nproposed realization projection to its accepted atom or atoms. Work inside an\naccepted boundary cites the existing Prime basis rather than recreating it.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FRecursive%20Prime%20And%20Root%20Conservation%20%28%60STDO-UP-003%60%29",
          "start_line": 1017
        }
      ],
      "key": "recursive_prime_root_conservation",
      "statement": "Contract each candidate atom and then complete resulting family. Local irreducibility/conformance does not prove global Prime where identity/authority/function/lifecycle/topology/effect/projection meaning duplicates. Preserve root authority and every retained relation; fewer files/functions/operations/surfaces cannot compensate rival truth/authority. Evidence includes full candidate family; each stable atom identity, irreducible relation, domain and falsifier; whole-family contraction; before/after meaning/authority; accepted loss; and total projection-to-accepted-atoms mapping.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["design_ontology", "design_boundary", "architectural_carrier_set"],
      "conditions": ["A design projection is made under the adopted Ontology profile."],
      "exceptions": ["Intentional omission/flattening requires declared accepted loss and failure condition.", "Implementation branches/test expectations need not be individually enumerated in Ontology when traceable through requirements plus accepted design."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1044,
          "quote": "The binding names its Ontology source and the laws preserved. Intentional\nomission or flattening declares accepted loss and a failure condition. Target\ndesign may add structural HOW, but cannot originate rival semantic meaning.\nA public operation, message, transition, carrier or effect untraceable through\naccepted design to the Ontology cannot enter the active line. Implementation\nbranches and test expectations trace to requirements plus accepted design;\nthey preserve the Ontology without needing individual enumeration in it.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F4B.%20Ontology-First%20Design%20Rule%2FOntology%20Projection%20Law",
          "start_line": 1038
        }
      ],
      "key": "ontology_projection_preservation",
      "statement": "Apply Faithful projection from named accepted Ontology preserving identity, relationship, lifecycle, authority, function and effect laws. Targets include domain/class, sequence/state views; authority/effect matrices; IACS; APIs/operation registers/SDK/CLI; schemas/codecs/manifests/catalogs; architecture/modules; and implementation/test/proof through accepted design and requirements. Name source/laws; target design may add HOW but no rival meaning. Untraceable public operation/message/transition/carrier/effect cannot enter active line.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["prime_semantic_atom", "architectural_carrier_set", "design_boundary"],
      "conditions": ["Prime profile applies to top-level realization units."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1083,
          "quote": "A top-level realization unit is **Prime-conformant** only when it projects one\nor more accepted Prime atoms without introducing, duplicating, or\nreinterpreting semantic authority. A topological or effect boundary must first\nbe derived and accepted as a Prime atom. Source-code size and one-to-one\ncorrespondence with an atom are immaterial.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F5.%20Prime%20Law",
          "start_line": 1079
        }
      ],
      "key": "prime_realization_law",
      "statement": "Derive atoms from logically complete candidate Ontology before top-level units; whole-family Prime supports Ontology acceptance. Design/IACS/modules/functions/schemas/tests project accepted atoms, not originate meaning. Prime-conformance applies to functions/classes/carrier types/top-level schemas/modules; typed closure alone does not justify new top-level type. Unit must project accepted atoms without introducing/duplicating/reinterpreting authority; topological/effect boundaries first require accepted atoms, regardless of code size or one-to-one mapping. Typical lawful new boundaries are admitted graph topology/branch, typed carrier transform, effect, validation/admission or projection. Units solely shortening calls, aggregating unrelated convenience, renaming old interfaces, wrapping/shuttling, hiding mutation/fallback/orchestration, naming payload variations lacking authority, publishing internal detail without irreducibility, mirroring slight field variation or multiplying types for typing discomfort are nonconformant. Prefer composition, existing lawful functions and fewer sharper boundaries/families. Aim is preventing fragmentation/helper sprawl, not minimum lines.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["design_boundary", "prime_semantic_atom"],
      "conditions": ["Reviewing decomposition or Prime contraction."],
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1129,
          "quote": "Review cuts, realization units, runtime modules, and work items are distinct\nboundaries. They may relate many-to-one or one-to-many and must not be forced\ninto one-to-one decomposition for administrative convenience.\n\nPrime review accounts for governance cost as well as implementation count.\nContraction is not successful when it increases authority centers, maintained\ntruth surfaces, acceptance boundaries, dependency cycles, manually reconciled\nprojections, or review burden. Evidence remains proportional to semantic\nchange and risk; this rule does not require one artifact or review per concern.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F5.%20Prime%20Law%2FBoundary%20And%20Governance%20Cost%20%28%60STDO-UP-005%60%29",
          "start_line": 1121
        }
      ],
      "key": "boundary_and_governance_cost",
      "statement": "Review cuts, realization units, runtime modules and work items are distinct, may map many-to-one/one-to-many, and must not be forced one-to-one administratively. Count governance cost as well as implementation count. Contraction is unsuccessful if it increases authority centers, truth surfaces, acceptance boundaries, cycles, manual reconciliation or review burden. Evidence is proportional to semantic change/risk; no artifact/review per concern is required.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
    {
      "applies_to_keys": ["architectural_carrier_set", "design_ontology"],
      "conditions": ["Defining a schema, carrier family or typed public boundary under the adopted IACS profile."],
      "exceptions": ["When co_evolution_admissible(B), Ontology, carrier evidence, implementation and tests may develop together, with acceptance/reconciliation before promotion/closure."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1169,
          "quote": "1. cite the accepted Ontology and function-derivation evidence\n2. declare the Irreducible Architectural Carrier Set\n3. map each carrier to the Ontology identity, lifecycle, function, authority,\n   effect, or projection law it carries\n4. declare which carriers are authoritative and which are downstream\n5. treat every other shape as a Subordinate Payload by default\n6. keep subordinate payload detail private unless it passes the Promotion Test\n7. reconcile the typed implementation to that carrier set before claiming\n   design-method closure",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md#Design%20Module%20Method%2F5A.%20Irreducible%20Architectural%20Carrier%20Set%20Rule",
          "start_line": 1161
        }
      ],
      "key": "iacs_derivation_and_closure",
      "statement": "Derive IACS from accepted Ontology before naming subordinate payloads/modules; it should precede helper-result/internal-branch naming. Branch payloads, persistence detail, read rows or typing-only field groupings do not automatically justify top-level carriers. Evidence cites accepted Ontology/function derivation, declares IACS, maps each carrier to carried identity/lifecycle/function/authority/effect/projection law, distinguishes authoritative/downstream, defaults all other shapes to subordinate, keeps details private unless Promotion Test passes, and reconciles implementation before closure. IACS cannot replace Ontology or originate entity/function/lifecycle/authority meaning. Undeclared accepted Ontology or IACS means schema not design-method complete. Co-evolution may expose missing meaning but cannot self-ratify; accept Ontology/IACS and reconcile before promotion/closure. In gated mode accept unresolved/contradictory/nonequivalent affected relation before retained implementation establishes it.",
      "uncertainty": "Full Promotion Test is not supplied."
    }
  ],
